  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.9.1 - CCLabel works on Linux and macOS desktop again: from 2.6.0 to 2.9.0 the first label there threw TypeInitializationException. No API changes. Labels there draw at about two-thirds of the font size, as they did in the 2.5.10 Linux and macOS packages.\n2.9.0 - The last nullable reference type annotations (the director and scheduler, the platform code, the embeddable view, the controls, the scroll views and the CCB reader), so the engine and Box2D are annotated throughout, apart from the deprecated zlib port. It also fixes bugs found while converting; some failures now throw ArgumentException, InvalidOperationException or InvalidDataException instead of NullReferenceException, and a few fixes change behavior. Zlib-compressed TMX layers decompress with System.IO.Compression, and the bundled zlib port (Cocos2D.Compression.Zlib) is obsolete; 3.0 removes it. Apart from nullability and that deprecation, no public API changed. Read the CHANGELOG's Upgrading notes before updating.\n- See https://github.com/Cocos2D-Mono/cocos2d-mono for the full changelog.",
